{"title":"Sights & Sounds","description":"Picture, sound and video clues: animal calls, famous voices, flags, landmarks, paintings and space launches (free public-domain and Creative Commons media from Wikimedia Commons and NASA)","selected":false,"media":true,"categories":[{"name":"Who's Making That Noise?","clues":[{"q":"Cock-a-doodle-doo! This farm bird is the one sounding off.","a":"Rooster","media":{"kind":"audio","url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/0d/Medium_rooster_crowing.ogg/Medium_rooster_crowing.ogg.mp3","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain, alys"},"alt":["chicken","cockerel"]},{"q":"This farm animal that gives us milk sounds just like this.","a":"Cow","media":{"kind":"audio","url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a5/Single_Cow_Moo.ogg/Single_Cow_Moo.ogg.mp3","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0, MichaeltheFox8621"},"alt":["cattle"]},{"q":"Woof! Man's best friend is making this racket.","a":"Dog","media":{"kind":"audio","url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a2/Barking_of_a_dog.ogg/Barking_of_a_dog.ogg.mp3","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0, Amada44"},"alt":["puppy"]},{"q":"This wild cousin of the dog howls to its pack at night.","a":"Wolf","media":{"kind":"audio","url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/87/Wolf_howls.ogg/Wolf_howls.ogg.mp3","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"},"alt":["wolves"]},{"q":"The largest animal on land makes this trumpeting call.","a":"Elephant","media":{"kind":"audio","url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/40/Elephant_voice_-_trumpeting.ogg/Elephant_voice_-_trumpeting.ogg.mp3","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, CC0"}}]},{"name":"Famous Voices","clues":[{"q":"In 1927 this inventor of the phonograph recited the rhyme he had first recorded 50 years before.","a":"Thomas Edison","media":{"kind":"audio","url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/63/Thomas_Edison_Mary_had_lamb.ogg/Thomas_Edison_Mary_had_lamb.ogg.mp3","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"},"alt":["Edison"]},{"q":"This astronaut said these words as he stepped onto the Moon in 1969.","a":"Neil Armstrong","media":{"kind":"audio","url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e0/Phrase_de_Neil_Armstrong.oga/Phrase_de_Neil_Armstrong.oga.mp3","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain, NASA"},"alt":["Armstrong"]},{"q":"This president called December 7, 1941, \"a date which will live in infamy.\"","a":"Franklin D. Roosevelt","media":{"kind":"audio","url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/46/1941_Roosevelt_speech_pearlharbor_p1.ogg/1941_Roosevelt_speech_pearlharbor_p1.ogg.mp3","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"},"alt":["FDR","Roosevelt","Franklin Roosevelt"]},{"q":"\"Houston, we've had a problem\" was radioed from this Apollo mission in 1970.","a":"Apollo 13","media":{"kind":"audio","url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/28/Apollo13problem.ogg/Apollo13problem.ogg.mp3","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain, NASA"},"alt":["13"]},{"q":"In 1958 this president's Christmas message became the first voice broadcast from a satellite in space.","a":"Dwight D. Eisenhower","media":{"kind":"audio","url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/cf/SCORE_Audio.ogg/SCORE_Audio.ogg.mp3","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"},"alt":["Eisenhower","Ike","Dwight Eisenhower"]}]},{"name":"Name That Flag","clues":[{"q":"A red circle on white flies for this island nation.","a":"Japan","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Flag_of_Japan.svg/1280px-Flag_of_Japan.svg.png","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"}},{"q":"A red maple leaf marks the flag of this country.","a":"Canada","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg/1280px-Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg.png","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"}},{"q":"The motto \"Ordem e Progresso\" crosses the starry globe on this South American country's flag.","a":"Brazil","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Flag_of_Brazil.svg/1280px-Flag_of_Brazil.svg.png","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"}},{"q":"A red and blue taegeuk sits in the middle of this Asian country's flag.","a":"South Korea","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Flag_of_South_Korea.svg/1280px-Flag_of_South_Korea.svg.png","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"},"alt":["Korea","Republic of Korea"]},{"q":"A Maasai shield and two spears appear on the flag of this East African country.","a":"Kenya","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Flag_of_Kenya.svg/1280px-Flag_of_Kenya.svg.png","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"}}]},{"name":"Famous Landmarks","clues":[{"q":"This Paris tower was built for the World's Fair of 1889.","a":"Eiffel Tower","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Tour_Eiffel_Wikimedia_Commons.jpg/1280px-Tour_Eiffel_Wikimedia_Commons.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain, Benh LIEU SONG"},"alt":["Eiffel","Tour Eiffel"]},{"q":"A gift from France, she has stood in New York Harbor since 1886.","a":"Statue of Liberty","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Statue_of_Liberty_7.jpg/1280px-Statue_of_Liberty_7.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain, Elcobbola"},"alt":["Lady Liberty","Liberty"]},{"q":"The only one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World still standing.","a":"Great Pyramid of Giza","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Kheops-Pyramid.jpg/1280px-Kheops-Pyramid.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 2.5, Nina"},"alt":["Great Pyramid","pyramid of Giza","pyramids","pyramid of Khufu"]},{"q":"Shah Jahan built this white marble tomb in Agra for his wife.","a":"Taj Mahal","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Taj_Mahal_%28Edited%29.jpeg/1280px-Taj_Mahal_%28Edited%29.jpeg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0, Yann; edited by Jim Carter"}},{"q":"This 15th-century Inca citadel sits high in the Andes of Peru.","a":"Machu Picchu","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Machu_Picchu%2C_Peru.jpg/1280px-Machu_Picchu%2C_Peru.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 2.0, Pedro Szekely"}}]},{"name":"Masterpieces","clues":[{"q":"Leonardo da Vinci painted this famous smile.","a":"Mona Lisa","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Mona_Lisa%2C_by_Leonardo_da_Vinci%2C_from_C2RMF_retouched.jpg/1280px-Mona_Lisa%2C_by_Leonardo_da_Vinci%2C_from_C2RMF_retouched.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"},"alt":["La Gioconda","Gioconda"]},{"q":"Vincent van Gogh painted this swirling night sky in 1889.","a":"The Starry Night","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Van_Gogh_-_Starry_Night_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Van_Gogh_-_Starry_Night_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"},"alt":["Starry Night"]},{"q":"Hokusai's giant wave rolls in front of this snowy Japanese mountain.","a":"Mount Fuji","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Tsunami_by_hokusai_19th_century.jpg/1280px-Tsunami_by_hokusai_19th_century.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"},"alt":["Fuji","Fujiyama"]},{"q":"This Dutch painter from Delft gave us \"Girl with a Pearl Earring.\"","a":"Johannes Vermeer","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/1665_Girl_with_a_Pearl_Earring.jpg/1280px-1665_Girl_with_a_Pearl_Earring.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"},"alt":["Vermeer"]},{"q":"This Norwegian artist painted \"The Scream.\"","a":"Edvard Munch","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Edvard_Munch%2C_1893%2C_The_Scream%2C_oil%2C_tempera_and_pastel_on_cardboard%2C_91_x_73_cm%2C_National_Gallery_of_Norway.jpg/1280px-Edvard_Munch%2C_1893%2C_The_Scream%2C_oil%2C_tempera_and_pastel_on_cardboard%2C_91_x_73_cm%2C_National_Gallery_of_Norway.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain"},"alt":["Munch"]}]},{"name":"Space Videos","clues":[{"q":"In July 1969 this NASA mission landed the first people on the Moon.","a":"Apollo 11","media":{"kind":"video","url":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/Apollo_11_Intro_720p/Apollo_11_Intro_720p~medium.mp4","start":0,"end":25,"credit":"NASA (public domain)"}},{"q":"Released from the space shuttle in 1990, this telescope is named for an American astronomer.","a":"Hubble Space Telescope","media":{"kind":"video","url":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/GSFC_20080822_HST_m10235_Deploy/GSFC_20080822_HST_m10235_Deploy~medium.mp4","start":0,"end":23,"credit":"NASA (public domain)"},"alt":["Hubble"]},{"q":"This NASA rover touched down in Mars's Jezero Crater in February 2021.","a":"Perseverance","media":{"kind":"video","url":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/JPL-20210218-M2020f-0003-Perseverance%20Landing%20Wrap%20v2/JPL-20210218-M2020f-0003-Perseverance%20Landing%20Wrap%20v2~medium.mp4","start":10,"end":40,"credit":"NASA (public domain)"},"alt":["Percy","Perseverance rover"]},{"q":"NASA's new Moon program is named for this Greek goddess, Apollo's twin sister.","a":"Artemis","media":{"kind":"video","url":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/Artemis%20I%20Launch%202022%20CU%20tracking%20from%20Press%20Site_compressed/Artemis%20I%20Launch%202022%20CU%20tracking%20from%20Press%20Site_compressed~medium.mp4","start":45,"end":75,"credit":"NASA (public domain)"}},{"q":"NASA's three-letter abbreviation for a spacewalk.","a":"EVA","media":{"kind":"video","url":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/jsc2022m000280_US_EVA_82_Animation_221203/jsc2022m000280_US_EVA_82_Animation_221203~medium.mp4","start":0,"end":25,"credit":"NASA (public domain)"},"alt":["extravehicular activity"]}]}],"finals":[{"category":"Space Sounds","q":"Launched in 1977 and now beyond the Sun's bubble, this NASA probe carries a golden record of Earth's sounds.","a":"Voyager 1","alt":["Voyager","Voyager 2","Voyager I"]}]}